@startuml
left to right direction

title Use Case Diagram for AI-Powered Analysis & Insights System

:Client: as Client
:SystemAdmin: as SysAdmin
:FInancialAdvisor: as FAdvisor
:AISystem: as AISys

rectangle "System" {
  usecase "CFR001: View Financial Insights Dashboard" as CFR001
  usecase "SAFR001: Manage Analysis Parameters" as SAFR001
  usecase "FAFR002: View Client Intervention Alerts" as FAFR002
  usecase "CFR003: View Financial Predictions" as CFR003
  usecase "CFR004: Receive Personalized Recommendations" as CFR004
  usecase "CFR005: Manage Recommendation Preferences" as CFR005
  usecase "CFR006: View Spending Limit Alerts" as CFR006
  usecase "CFR007: View Investment Opportunities" as CFR007
  usecase "CFR008: Access Personalized Dashboard" as CFR008
  usecase "CFR10: Manage Relationship with Financial Advisors" as CFR10

  SysAdmin --> SAFR001 : Configure system parameters for compliance.

  Client -> CFR001 : View dashboard.
  Client -> CFR003 : View predictions.
  Client -> CFR004 : Receive recommendations.
  Client -> CFR005 : Manage preferences.
  Client -> CFR006 : View alerts.
  Client -> CFR007 : View opportunities.
  Client -> CFR008 : Access dashboard.
  Client -> SAFR001 : Adjust parameters (via SysAdmin).
  
  FAdvisors --> FAFR002: Manage client alerts and mentoring sessions.
  FAdvisors --> FAFR003: View predictive analytics for clients.
  FAdvisors --> AIFR008: Generate intervention recommendations.

  AISys <|-- SAFR001 : Implements analysis parameter management.
  AISys <|-- CFR004 : Generates personalized recommendations.
  AISys <|-- CFR006 : Alerts on spending limits.
  AISys <|-- CFR007 : Analyzes investment opportunities.
  AISys <|-- AIFR003: Spends limit alerts based on patterns.
  AISys <|-- AIFR004: Personalized recommendations aligned with profiles.
  AISys <|-- AIFR005: Investment opportunity analyses per risk profile.
  
  Client --> AISys : Provide data for analysis (e.g., spending, investments).
}

@enduml